[bold,italic,double-underline]Field Manual 42-B: Interdimensional Incident Response[]

[bold,underline]Preamble[]

This manual describes standard operating procedure for [bold]Class-III multiverse[]
[bold]incursions[], as adopted by the [italic]Intergalactic Committee on Narrative Integrity[]
(ICNI). All personnel are required to read it twice, sign the waiver, and
memorize Section 4 before their next shift.

[dim]│ [][dim,italic]"The universe is not only stranger than we imagine, it is stranger than we can[]
[dim]│ [][dim,italic]be reimbursed for."[]
[dim]│ []
[dim]│ [][dim,italic]— Admiral Ackbar, 2387 budget hearing[]
[dim]│ []
[dim]│ │ [][dim,italic]Accounting note: next time, please file form [][bold,dim,italic]W-42B[][dim,italic] in triplicate.[]

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[bold,underline]Section 1 — Crossover Classification[]

The following incursion types have been observed in the last [strike]fiscal quarter[]
epoch:

┌───────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────┐
│ [bold]Class[] │ [bold]              Example               [] │ [bold]Threat Level[] │
├───────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┤
│ Alpha │ Gandalf at Comic-Con                 │ Low          │
├───────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┤
│ Beta  │ Spock attending a quidditch match    │ Medium       │
├───────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────┤
│ Gamma │ A TARDIS inside a Death Star reactor │ CRITICAL     │
└───────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────┘

See [underline]the full classification taxonomy[][dim] (https://example.invalid/icni/taxonomy)[] for
additional detail, or browse the quick reference at
[underline]https://example.invalid/icni/quick-ref[][dim] (https://example.invalid/icni/quick-ref)[].

[bold,underline]Section 2 — Initial Response[]

Upon detecting an incursion, operatives should:

1. Confirm the breach using the [yellow]multiverse-scan --now[] command.
2. Assess threat level per Section 1.
3. Notify your local liaison. [bold]Do not[] attempt to resolve Alpha-class incursions
   personally — they typically resolve themselves once coffee is offered.
4. File an incident report, even if the incident was "just a cat".

[bold]Example Scan Output[]

  $ multiverse-scan[cyan] --now[]
  [ok] scanning timelines 1..2^64
  [warn] anomaly at (42, 7, 1977)
  [critical] The One Ring detected inside a replicator unit

If the output looks garbled, try the unflagged variant:

  [yellow]multiverse-scan[]

Operators with code access prefer the Python wrapper, which returns structured
anomalies and mirrors the CLI flags:

  [magenta]from[] multiverse [magenta]import[] scanner
  
  scan [magenta]=[] scanner.scan([cyan]now[][magenta]=[][yellow]True[], [cyan]depth[][magenta]=[][yellow]64[])
  [magenta]for[] anomaly [magenta]in[] scan.anomalies:
      [cyan]print[]([magenta]f[][green]"[[]{anomaly.severity}[green]] []{anomaly.description}[green]"[])

[bold,underline]Section 3 — Field Kit[]

Operatives carry the following items at all times:

• A [italic]sonic screwdriver[] (standard issue)
• One (1) [yellow]phaser[], set to stun
• A small notebook labelled [bold]Don't Panic[]
• Emergency rations, consisting of:
  • Lembas bread
  • Replicator chits
  • A single chocolate frog, for morale

    Morale is critical on extended assignments. Personnel who neglect their
    chocolate frog ration have been observed to sulk, at which point rescue
    teams report a measurable drop in [italic]snark throughput[].

The kit manifest is distributed as YAML so replicator units with only minimal
parsing capability can still honor a request:

  [red]kit[]:
    [red]standard[]:
      - [green]sonic screwdriver[]
      - [green]phaser[]
    [red]morale[]:
      [red]chocolate_frog[]: [yellow]1[]
      [red]notebook[]: [green]"Don't Panic"[]

[bold]Escalation Chain[]

Incidents escalate in the following order:

1. Field operative
2. Shift supervisor
3. Regional coordinator
  1. First deputy
  2. Second deputy (Tuesdays only)
4. ICNI council

[image: Official ICNI seal][dim] (https://example.invalid/icni/seal.png)[]

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[bold,underline]Appendix A — Poetry Corner[]

By long-standing tradition, every manual concludes with a verse. The following
was composed by R2-D2 during his tenure as guest editor:

Beep boop beep, the stars align,
The Force and phasers intertwine,
One does not simply walk to warp,
So set your course, and mind the sharp.

[italic]End of document.[]
